 "recognition_note": "The exact six supplied CDRs match sequence set 25/29 in WO2023056473A1 (published 2023-04-06), which the ordered clone table and 2D9/3E8 cross-check assign to HAstV mAb 3H4. Moreno-Contreras et al. (first public 2018-10-22) assigns 3H4 escape K504E; the pre-cutoff 5EWO numbering record maps viral K504 to supplied A/B:75. No 3H4-spike complex was found. The same variable-domain sequence is also historically associated with HC19, so recognition rests specifically on the exact astrovirus patent sequence set, its clone ordering, and the stipulated binding pair.",
 "what_separated_them": "Exact clone identification plus clone-specific K504E escape is the only Tier A localization and assigns 0.95 total probability to the K75 group. Within that group Tier A does not define a boundary: C5 gets a modest compactness/chemistry prior, while C3 and C8 are exact duplicate advocacy footprints and therefore split the broad-boundary mass equally. The remaining candidates are a low-probability allosteric or identity-failure tail supported only by other-antibody precedent.",
